  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Mix all to a stiff paste, moistening with a little milk if necessary, but be careful, for milk will make the pudding heavy.",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "text": "The eggs and milk should be stirred into the ingredients after they have been thoroughly mixed together, and last of all the brandy and liqueur.",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "text": "This pudding will take ten hours to boil, and is large enough for a party of sixteen.",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "text": "For sauce: Put ten yolks of eggs in a stew-pan, four ounces of sugar, one pint of milk.",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir over the fire in a \"bain marie\" (double boiler) till a rich custard has been formed; add a claret glass of Noyeau; strain the sauce and serve hot.",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Instead of Noyeau three-quarters of a pint of Madeira may be used.",
      "section": null
    }
  ],
